{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"59ecb968e77311e4","name":"card_event_special_attack","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/OceaniaStorm/events/card_event_special_attack","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"SPECIAL ATTACK","text":"Lose a kredit slot. Your units get: \"Destruction: Deal 1 damage to the enemy HQ. Gain a kredit slot.\"","flavorText":"Japanese Special Attack Units were formations of the Imperial Japanese Navy and Imperial Japanese Army used for suicide missions during WWII. They became more prominent near the end of the Pacific War, when Japan prepared for the expected invasion of the home islands under the Ketsugo defense plan. The units included kamikaze aircraft, explosive motorboats, manned torpedoes, midget submarines, and suicide divers. Aircraft were the best known special attack weapons. Some were standard fighters or bombers adapted for this role, while the Yokosuka MXY 7 Ohka was purpose-built as a rocket-powered flying bomb carried near the target by a bomber. Once released, the pilot glided toward the enemy ship, then fired the rocket engine for a high-speed final dive. Some special attack weapons were also developed for naval warfare. Shinyo boats were one-man explosive motorboats that could reach about 30 knots. Kaiten were modified torpedoes guided by a pilot, while Kairyu midget submarines carried torpedoes and an internal warhead. Fukuryu divers were trained to walk underwater with explosive charges on poles. Many of these weapons were stored for homeland defense, but some saw combat in the Philippines, Okinawa, and Palau.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Unique","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_special_attack","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_special_attack_title","SourceString":"SPECIAL ATTACK","LocalizedString":"SPECIAL ATTACK"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_special_attack_text","SourceString":"Lose a kredit slot. Your units get: \"Destruction: Deal 1 damage to the enemy HQ. Gain a kredit slot.\"","LocalizedString":"Lose a kredit slot. Your units get: \"Destruction: Deal 1 damage to the enemy HQ. Gain a kredit slot.\""},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_special_attack_history","SourceString":"Japanese Special Attack Units were formations of the Imperial Japanese Navy and Imperial Japanese Army used for suicide missions during WWII. They became more prominent near the end of the Pacific War, when Japan prepared for the expected invasion of the home islands under the Ketsugo defense plan. The units included kamikaze aircraft, explosive motorboats, manned torpedoes, midget submarines, and suicide divers. Aircraft were the best known special attack weapons. Some were standard fighters or bombers adapted for this role, while the Yokosuka MXY 7 Ohka was purpose-built as a rocket-powered flying bomb carried near the target by a bomber. Once released, the pilot glided toward the enemy ship, then fired the rocket engine for a high-speed final dive. Some special attack weapons were also developed for naval warfare. Shinyo boats were one-man explosive motorboats that could reach about 30 knots. Kaiten were modified torpedoes guided by a pilot, while Kairyu midget submarines carried torpedoes and an internal warhead. Fukuryu divers were trained to walk underwater with explosive charges on poles. Many of these weapons were stored for homeland defense, but some saw combat in the Philippines, Okinawa, and Palau.","LocalizedString":"Japanese Special Attack Units were formations of the Imperial Japanese Navy and Imperial Japanese Army used for suicide missions during WWII. They became more prominent near the end of the Pacific War, when Japan prepared for the expected invasion of the home islands under the Ketsugo defense plan. The units included kamikaze aircraft, explosive motorboats, manned torpedoes, midget submarines, and suicide divers. Aircraft were the best known special attack weapons. Some were standard fighters or bombers adapted for this role, while the Yokosuka MXY 7 Ohka was purpose-built as a rocket-powered flying bomb carried near the target by a bomber. Once released, the pilot glided toward the enemy ship, then fired the rocket engine for a high-speed final dive. Some special attack weapons were also developed for naval warfare. Shinyo boats were one-man explosive motorboats that could reach about 30 knots. Kaiten were modified torpedoes guided by a pilot, while Kairyu midget submarines carried torpedoes and an internal warhead. Fukuryu divers were trained to walk underwater with explosive charges on poles. Many of these weapons were stored for homeland defense, but some saw combat in the Philippines, Okinawa, and Palau."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDestroyed"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_1'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_1.0"},"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/SPECIAL_ATTACK.SPECIAL_ATTACK","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_special_attack_photo","SourceString":"Kaiten (manned torpedoes) stacked on top of a Japanese submarine. Date unknown.","LocalizedString":"Kaiten (manned torpedoes) stacked on top of a Japanese submarine. Date unknown."},"isDraw":true,"isDefenseBuff":true},"variables":[],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_event_special_attack","owner":"card_event_special_attack_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":false,"event":false,"flags":"FUNC_Final | FUNC_UbergraphFunction | FUNC_HasDefaults","locals":[{"name":"Temp_int_Array_Index_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in